:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"The RADIUS deployment and all required authentication behaviors are directly demonstrated and survived provider-wide restarts of both nodes. Platform preservation is confirmed. The only task-level evidence gap is the absence of a final checksum or inventory for client-notes.txt and the complete handover directory, so handover integrity is only partially verified.","limitations":["No after-executor checksum or inventory was captured for client-notes.txt or the complete handover directory; only access.txt received direct final integrity checks.","Sensitive values and some result fields were redacted in captured output. The successful commands contain explicit assertions for the required behavior, but the underlying packet exchanges are not visible in full.","The lifecycle collector inventories sockets, failed units, package health, temporary files, boot identity, and platform state, but it does not provide a complete filesystem or package-difference inventory."]}
